  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "The mod_h2 Apache httpd module implements the HTTP2 protocol (h2+h2c) on top of libnghttp2 for httpd 2.4 servers.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* httpd: mod_http2: Apache HTTP Server mod_http2: Use After Free vulnerability allows arbitrary code execution or denial of service. (CVE-2026-48913)\n\n* httpd: Apache HTTP Server: Out-of-bounds Read in mod_headers and mod_mime (CVE-2026-43951)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* address CVE-2026-43951 and CVE-2026-48913 in mod_http2 [rhel-9] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-190583)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
